<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prättigau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prättigau is an Alpine valley of the Landquart river in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. Held by the counts of Toggenburg and later largely by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, its communities joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> in 1436. In 1622, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, its people rose against Austrian occupation in the Prättigau uprising.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prattigau.jpg" alt="Prättigau" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adrian Michael · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%A4ttigau_S.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
